WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.510
In 1900, 41 percent of the
US workforce worked on farms.

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.830
By 1930, 21.5 percent.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.390
By 1970, 4 percent.

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.070
By 2000, just 1.9 percent.

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.070
Did Americans eat less?

6
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.590
Was the food imported?

7
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.250
Did farm workers just work longer hours?

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.230
How did fewer farmers feed more people?

9
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.630
In this mission, you'll trace
three great changes in farming,

10
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.730
from England's fenced fields to today.

11
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.570
Then you'll follow one wheat
variety from Japan to Mexico,

12
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.350
then on to Pakistan and India, and
weigh the gains against the losses.

13
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: explain how fewer
farmers came to feed more people.
